This was carved from softcut using Essdee tools.

The coelacanth is a living fossil, a design unchanged in 400 million years. This lobe-finned fish  was thought to be extinct until specimens were discovered in 1938 off the coast of South Africa.

I have printed this on hand-torn wenzhou paper and also seawhite cartridge paper.

